  "title": "The faces a handle uses are a property of its port relation",
  "subject": "Which faces each handle of a census of 305 creates through on a ladder",
  "conclusion": "Across 305 handles from 24 non-planar knot spaces, every port order on a ladder, the faces a handle creates through are decided by its port relation alone: whether a pair of its points pins the face's barred state while each single point keeps the face's claims. Nine signatures occur; census 58 uses its own arc exactly when the bottom port is a third point of its two lines sharing two points.",
